+# The document arrives under a contract nobody told the model
+
+Status: ready-for-agent
+
+Blocks 05, which re-runs the pass this is measured by.
+
+The first log pass on the graph held **24 of 90** on `gpt-oss:20b`. Rescored on the document the engine would write, the **50** determined runs that emitted one go from **7 to 30** held. Most of the failures are the contract between the emitted form, the prompt and the scorer -- not the reading of the sentence. Four defects, every one of them decidable without a provider:
+
+| # | what | where | what it costs |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | the scorer charges for a shape that writes the same row | `log_evaluation._difference` | 23 of 50 determined runs |
+| 2 | the prompt forbids `assumed`, the form requires a value and the set expects `assumed` | `logger.LOGGING` | every block holding a value nobody mentioned |
+| 3 | a refusal ends the run, where the planner's goes back to the model | `logger.build.validate` | the run, scored as *not run* when nothing parsed |
+| 4 | the exclusion vocabulary is in no prompt, no brief and no tool answer | `logger.brief` | U13-U16, and false exclusions in the other half |
+
+**The form requires every value in a block.** `tools.strict_schema` marks every property required, and `PerformedBlock` requires `rounds`, `rounds_source`, `rest` and `rest_source` on its own. A block can be left out whole; nothing inside one can. So *"solo 2 serie di militari"* has to carry the rest nobody mentioned and the reps nobody mentioned, and `assumed` at the prescribed value is the only true label for them -- CONTEXT.md § Provenance, and `log._nothing_assumed_the_prescription_does_not_say` refuses only an `assumed` the prescription **contradicts**.
+
+The prompt says the opposite twice -- *"Never `assumed`: that is the engine's"* and *"A value nobody gave is left out, not filled in"* -- and then licenses it two bullets later for a substitution. The set has expected `assumed` on those fields since it was written (U2, U5, U9-U12, U17, U18).
+
+## What to build
+
+**1. The determined half is scored on the document the engine would write.**
+
+- `workout_id`, `report` and `proposed_exclusion` stay compared on the emitted document: they are claims only it makes, and `to_performed` returns blocks.
+- Blocks are compared after `log.to_performed`, on both sides, against the fixture -- `_produced` already resolves the expected document that way for the volume column.
+- **Order-insensitive where a prescription backs the document**, keyed by each block's set of exercise ids. `to_performed` appends the reported blocks first and the untouched prescribed ones after, so the resolved order is which blocks the user talked about and not the order of the session. With `workout_id: null` nothing is filled in, the order is the document's own, and it is compared -- *"poi"* is what makes U8 two blocks in sequence.
+- Provenance keeps its teeth: a `rest_source` of `reported` where the user said nothing still fails, because the resolved block carries it.
+- What this gives up is weighed and paid for: a document that restates the whole prescription resolves to the same written row as the empty one, and would now hold. It is counted in `_notes` instead, beside the questions-asked-anyway line -- *N of M runs restated the prescription; not scored, and not free either*.
+- `docs/logging/eval-set.md` § How to read a row says a document restating the unchanged parts *"is wrong about what the agent should emit"*. That stays true of what the agent is asked for and is no longer what it is scored on; the file has to say so, or the set and the scorer are two standards. **No row changes** -- 05 is explicit that the invariants are the set's own rows.
+
+**2. `LOGGING` states the contract the form imposes.**
+
+- Delete *"Never `assumed`"* and *"A value nobody gave is left out, not filled in"*.
+- Say it at the granularity the shape has: a block you do not mention is left out; a block you do mention carries **every** value, so a number the user never gave is the prescription's own number labelled `assumed`, and `reported` on it is the one lie nothing downstream can catch.
+- Keep the two rules that are already right: an `assumed` number must be the prescribed one, and a load is never `assumed`.
+- `test_the_logging_prompt_carries_the_rules_this_ticket_decided` grows the new rules; it is the test that would have caught this.
+
+**3. A refused document goes back to the model, once.**
+
+- `logger.ATTEMPTS = 2` and a `FEEDBACK`-shaped message naming the refusal, mirroring `planner.REFUSED_TURN`/`FEEDBACK`. The prompt says how many attempts there are, as `PLANNING` does.
+- **Both refusals go back**: `log.LogError` from `parse` as well as `log.LogRejected` from `validate`. Today a shape error closes the run with `document: None`, which `log_evaluation._invoked` raises on -- a row in the *not run* column with nothing to score.
+- Routed back to `logger`, not to `emit`: the commonest refusal is an `assumed` value the prescription contradicts, and the number that fixes it is one only `prescribed_workout` has.
+- The run is closed `REFUSED` only once the attempts are spent, and the record is still written exactly once. `test_a_refused_document_ends_the_run_as_refused` becomes *after the attempts are spent*, and a second test covers the refusal that is fixed on the retry.
+- The call budget already terminates this: with `spent >= budget` the retry turn is bound no tools, answers in prose, and `after_logger` sends it to `emit`.
+
+**4. The brief carries the two vocabularies, read from the data.**
+
+- `catalog.values(connection, "movement_pattern")` and `catalog.joint_values(connection)`, resolved once per run in `turn` through `tools.opened()` and passed into `brief` -- never a constant, for the reason `exclusions.classify` reads the same two tables and `trainer catalog` does not keep a copy of the twelve patterns.
+- Stated as the closed sets `proposed_exclusion.value` must come from, character for character, with no hint which of the two a report should land in: U13/U14 are the pair that measures exactly that.
+- An empty joint vocabulary is a state, not an omission: an unenriched catalog gets a brief saying only a pattern can be named, and `log_evaluation.missing` grows the same sentence -- four rows of the set cannot be answered without `loaded_joints`, and that is worth knowing before 90 runs rather than after.
+
+Leaving `movement_pattern` and `loaded_joints` out of `logger.KEEPS` is deliberate: the closed vocabulary is what these rows need, and per-exercise joints are context paid for on every turn with no failing row behind them. If 05's pass still misses U13-U16 with the vocabulary in the brief, that is where to look next.
+
+## What this may break
+
+The bar is 100% and `trainer eval` exits non-zero below it (`cli.py`), and ROADMAP.md § Risks already says that a model which cannot hold it with feedback is a finding about the model and not a reason to lower the bar. **Nothing here lowers it.** Three of the four changes make a correct agent scoreable; the fourth tells it something true that it was not told. What the pass comes to afterwards is 05's number to report, per row.
+
+Giving the model the exclusion vocabulary is the one change that can make a column worse: A5 and A12 expect **no** exclusion, and a named list is a list to pick from. The `false confidence` column is where that would show.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [ ] The 90 records of the failed pass, rescored by the new scorer offline, with the figure and the rows that moved written down here. The records hold the emitted document (`record.of` -> `performed`) and the questions, so this needs no provider and no model.
+- [ ] A document restating the whole prescription and the empty document score the same, and both hold U1.
+- [ ] A `rest_source` of `reported` on a value the report does not give still fails the document column.
+- [ ] Two blocks resolved in a different order hold against a prescription, and fail against `workout_id: null`.
+- [ ] A refused document is emitted again with the refusal in the context, and a run refused twice closes `REFUSED` with one record.
+- [ ] The brief names every movement pattern and every loaded joint the fixture's catalog holds, read from it; against a catalog with no enrichment it says so instead.
+- [ ] `trainer eval --suite log --only U13 --only U2` against a real provider, as the one end-to-end check this ticket pays for: two rows, one for the vocabulary and one for `assumed`. `prepared` points `TRAINER_DB` at its own copy, so what has to be true is that the database it copies holds the enriched catalog -- the joint vocabulary is enrichment. The 90-run pass stays 05's.
+- [ ] The full test suite and mypy are green.
+
+## Comments
+
+Found by the first pass of 05 against a real provider, 2026-09-22. The set was written blind in session 5 against `log.py` and `exclusions.py`, which is why it is the prompt and the scorer that are wrong about the shape and not the set: the rows were written from the code that resolves the document, and the emitted form grew a strict schema afterwards.
+
+Scoring on the resolved document is the same argument `_filled` already makes in the must-ask half -- *a block whose every value is `assumed` says it went as prescribed, so writing it out and leaving it out are the same document*. Half the suite has been reading it that way since it was built.
